# The last thing the seat check said, in one line: which seat, what it
# read, how far that was from the seat's own range and how much of the
# window carried one. The verdict alone is in Robot:Seat:* above; this
# is the reading behind it, including the answers that are not a
# verdict -- the check switched off, the seat outside the frame, too few
# pixels to say. Those used to live only in the daemon's terminal, which
# is not where the person looking at a stopped arm is.
record(stringin, "Robot:Seat:Msg")
{
    field(DESC, "Last seat check reading, 39 chars")
    field(VAL,  "")
}
